@@ -3,3 +3,24 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value that a JSON Pointer ([RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901))
+refers to inside a JSON document:
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+const doc = { order: { items: [{ sku: "A-1" }, { sku: "B-2" }] } };
+resolvePointer(doc, "/order/items/1/sku"); // "B-2"
+resolvePointer(doc, "");                   // the whole document
+```
+
+- The pointer must be a string in the RFC form: empty, or starting with `/`. The URI fragment form (`#/...`) is rejected.
+- `~1` and `~0` are unescaped to `/` and `~`; any other `~` makes the pointer invalid.
+- Array elements are addressed by index with no leading zeros. The `-` token names no element, so it does not resolve.
+- Only own properties of objects are members, so inherited names such as `/constructor` do not resolve.
+- Invalid pointers and pointers that do not resolve both throw a `JsonPointerError`, which is exported too.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
